## 👤 2. Identity & Access Control (IAM)

### The 3 Types of Access:
```
🔹 User Access = Regular people logging in
🔹 Privileged Access = Admins with extra power ⚡
🔹 Service Access = Apps/services talking to each other
```

### Core IAM Concepts:
| Concept | What It Means | Why It Matters |
|---------|--------------|----------------|
| **Authentication** | Proving who you are (password, MFA, biometrics) | Stops imposters |
| **Authorization** | What you're allowed to do after logging in | Prevents over-access |
| **Account Provisioning** | Creating/managing user accounts | Keeps access current |
| **Directory Services** | Central list of users/groups (like Azure AD) | Makes management easier |
| **Least Privilege** | Give only the access someone *needs* | Reduces damage if account is compromised |

### 🎯 Real-World Analogy:
> Think of IAM like an office building:
> - **Authentication** = Your badge gets you in the door
> - **Authorization** = Your badge only opens doors you need
> - **Privileged access** = Master key for facilities staff
> - **Service access** = The elevator talking to the security system

