## 🧹 3. Data & Media Sanitization

### Why sanitize? 
When you're done with data, you must **truly delete it** — not just "move to trash."

### Sanitization Methods:
| Method | How It Works | Best For |
|--------|-------------|----------|
| **Overwriting** | Writing new data over old data (1-7 passes) | Traditional hard drives |
| **Cryptographic Erase** | Deleting the encryption key = data becomes unreadable | Cloud storage, SSDs |
| **Degaussing** | Using strong magnet to scramble drive | Physical media (not cloud) |
| **Physical Destruction** | Shredding, incinerating | End-of-life hardware |

### 🧠 Memory Trick:
> **"Crypto-shredding"** = Delete the key, not the data. Like burning the map instead of the treasure.

### ⚠️ Cloud Challenge:
You often can't physically destroy cloud media. **Cryptographic erase is your best friend here.**

