## 🌐 4. Network Security

### Key Concepts:
```
🔸 Network Security Groups (NSGs) = Cloud firewalls
   • Rules that allow/deny traffic to VMs or subnets
   • Example: "Only allow port 443 from trusted IPs"

🔸 Traffic Inspection = Watching data packets for threats
   • Firewalls, IDS (detect), IPS (prevent)
   • Like a security camera for your network traffic

🔸 Geofencing = Virtual boundaries based on location
   • Block access from certain countries
   • Trigger alerts if login comes from unusual place

🔸 Zero Trust Network = "Never trust, always verify"
   • No automatic trust, even inside your network
   • Verify every request, every time
```

### 🎯 Simple Analogy:
> Zero Trust is like a high-security lab:
> - You badge in at the door ✅
> - Then you badge again for each room ✅
> - And again for each cabinet ✅
> - No one gets a "free pass"

