## 🖥️ 5. Virtualization Security

### Hypervisors (The "VM Managers"):
| Type | Description | Security Note |
|------|-------------|---------------|
| **Type 1 (Bare Metal)** | Runs directly on hardware (ESXi, Hyper-V) | More secure, fewer attack layers |
| **Type 2 (Hosted)** | Runs on top of an OS (VirtualBox, VMware Workstation) | More convenient, but extra attack surface |

### Other Virtualization Concepts:
```
🔹 Container Security (Docker, Kubernetes)
   • Lightweight, share OS kernel
   • Risk: If one container breaks out, others at risk
   • Protect with: Image scanning, runtime protection, network policies

🔹 Ephemeral Computing
   • Short-lived resources (auto-scale, serverless)
   • Challenge: Hard to monitor what you can't see for long
   • Solution: Log everything, automate security checks

🔹 Serverless (Lambda, Azure Functions)
   • You write code, provider runs it
   • Shared responsibility: You secure code & config; they secure infrastructure
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick:
> **"Hypervisor = Hotel Manager"**
> - Type 1: Manager owns the building (more control)
> - Type 2: Manager rents a floor (less control)
> - If the manager is compromised, all guests (VMs) are at risk

