## ⚠️ 6. Common Cloud Threats

### Top Threats (CSA Top 9 + more):
```
🚨 Data Breaches — Unauthorized access to sensitive data
🚨 Weak IAM — Poor access controls = easy target
🚨 Insecure APIs — Cloud apps talk via APIs; bad APIs = open doors
🚨 System Vulnerabilities — Unpatched software = hacker playground
🚨 Account Hijacking — Stolen credentials = attacker with your keys
🚨 Malicious Insiders — Trusted people doing bad things
🚨 APTs (Advanced Persistent Threats) — Patient, targeted attackers
🚨 Data Loss — Accidental deletion, corruption, or ransomware
🚨 Shared Tech Issues — Multi-tenant = your neighbor's problem could be yours
🚨 DoS/DDoS — Overwhelm services to make them crash
🚨 Abuse of Cloud Resources — Attackers using YOUR cloud to attack others
```

### 🎯 Quick Defense Checklist:
✅ Strong authentication (MFA everywhere)  
✅ Least privilege access  
✅ Regular patching  
✅ Encryption for sensitive data  
✅ Monitor logs and alerts  
✅ Test backups and recovery  

