## 🧼 7. Security Hygiene

### The Basics (Do These Consistently):
| Practice | What It Is | Why It Matters |
|----------|-----------|----------------|
| **Patching** | Updating software to fix known bugs | Closes doors hackers know about |
| **Baselining** | Setting a "secure default" configuration | Prevents misconfigurations |
| **Logging** | Recording what happens in your systems | You can't fix what you can't see |
| **Monitoring** | Watching logs/alerts for suspicious activity | Catch problems early |
| **Configuration Management** | Keeping systems consistent and documented | Reduces "snowflake servers" |

### 🧠 Memory Trick:
> **"Hygiene = Habits"**  
> Security isn't one big action — it's small, consistent habits:
> - Patch Tuesday? Do it.  
> - New server? Apply baseline.  
> - Strange log entry? Investigate.

